      "message": "fix(ui): \"Pick for WCS\" takes viewport picks in the default Model mode\n\nThe Setups page's WCS role draft leaves the toolbar's pick mode alone on\npurpose (it takes faces, edges and corners together), but the viewport\nsent a click to feature_click only in Face/Edge/Vertex mode. In the\ndefault Model mode with no operation open, every click selected the whole\nmodel and the draft never received a pick; the hover had the same gate.\n\ninteract::feature_routed now routes click and hover to the feature pick\nrule while wcs_pick::collecting, whatever geo_pick is. Disarmed or paused,\nthe mode's own click behaviour is back. Apply is unchanged: the undoable\nSetWcs, so a tilted frame is still placed and generation still refuses it\nby name (#1518).\n\nPinned by wcs_pick_click_tests::an_armed_row_takes_viewport_picks_from_the_default_model_mode,\nwhich arms the row from a fresh project and drives face, edge and corner\npicks and the hover through interact::pick_at / update_hover.\n\nFixes #1562\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
